<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Utility carcasses steady; Cutter not established. Demand light to moderate for light offerings. - USDA.</p>
<p>COW &amp; BULL CARCASS FOB WEST COAST 3.0 loads reported.</p>
<p>			  Lds     Price Range    Latest Estb. Mkt.</p>
<p>UT,brk 2-4 450#/up  1.0	55.00		 55.00</p>
<p>UT,bng 1-3 400#/up  2.0	59.00		 59.00</p>
<p>Cutter 1-2 350#/up				     58.00</p>
<p>Bulls YG 1 500#/up					 unq</p>
<p>BONELESS PROCESSING BEEF/BEEF TRIMMINGS 189.0  Loads Reported.</p>
<p>Lean boneless beef steady to firm in the Midwest, but Texas 2.00 to 3.00 higher on very light offerings; 85% and 65% generally steady. Demand and offerings light to moderate. Beef trimmings higher on moderate demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
